WEBVTT

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.220
This feels great!

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.160
Too light!  Light!  Light!

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.690
You're stepping on it too lightly, Capeta!

00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.650
You're supposed to step on it harder!

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:43.860
<b>Okay.</b>

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.210
You can do more than that!

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.710
Don't chicken out on the straight!

00:00:56.710 --> 00:01:00.000
Step on it!  Step on it!  And step on it some more!

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.660
Yeah, a bit more here.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.850
Capeta, 1 minute 45.583 seconds!

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.220
He's finally gotten within the 45-second range.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:10.220
He's still lukewarm.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.500
Our ace sure is tough.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.800
Your new driver... he sure is something.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.190
I heard he's going to debut in the 6th race.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:20.870
Oh, hello.

00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:21.850
Hi.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.180
He's going to be 16, after all.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.780
Once he gets his limited license,
he can finally debut in FSte races.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:30.870
All it means is that he can officially compete now.

00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:32.870
Well, I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:36.220
I wonder if he'll become the talk of the circuit like Minamoto last year.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.740
You look like you want to say something.

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.880
They're still too weak!

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:44.590
They don't have that spirit that goes zoom or bang!

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:47.130
Komazawa, get going and drive.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.020
How much do you think it's costing us
just to borrow this place for half a day?!

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.310
Y-Yes sir!

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.940
<i>Finally... I can finally fight him!</i>

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:54.080
Morning.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.000
Oh...

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.430
Are you going to school today?

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.530
Nope.  Persec.

00:03:58.530 --> 00:03:59.880
Well, I'm off!

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:00.350
Yeah.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.220
Oh yeah.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.920
I'm sorry, but could you ask Monami-chan for an autograph again?

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.360
I just couldn't say no.

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.650
Why don't you ask her yourself?

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.370
But if you could do me the favor...

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:11.920
Please?  Please?  Please?

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:12.400
Please?  Please?  Please?

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:13.000
Please?  Please?  Please?

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.730
It's because you go around boasting that you know her, right?

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:13.210
Capeta.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:14.920
Capeta!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.890
Oh, Nobu.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.270
It's not "Oh, Nobu."

00:05:21.270 --> 00:05:22.800
You have drool on your face.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.230
Your debut race in the FSte is coming up,
 so what's with that relaxed face?!

00:05:27.690 --> 00:05:28.870
Capeta.

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.000
You remember the three rules I gave you, right?

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:31.440
Okay.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.160
Rule number one.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:34.400
Finish the race.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.430
That's right.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.750
It may be obvious, but no crashes or retires.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:40.020
Rule number two.

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:41.040
Stand out.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.850
Yeah.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.720
Stand out from everyone and get yourself noticed.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.000
Things will be different once you leave a good impression in your debut race.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:50.770
Rule number three.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.620
Hey, you're getting off here, right?

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:54.930
You'll miss your stop!

00:05:55.850 --> 00:05:56.540
Huh?

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:57.850
Oh no!

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.740
Rule number three.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.220
Produce results!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.760
I'm sorry.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:07.320
<i>I wonder if he'll be okay without me around...</i>

00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:25.500
Hey, Capeta.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.430
Can you bring me a muffler?

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:29.960
The one on top of that shelf over there.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:34.560
It doesn't look like he's heard you.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.840
He's too caught up in his own work.

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:38.380
Hey, Capeta.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:42.890
Ow...

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.130
Your senior is calling you.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:49.810
What is it?

00:06:50.730 --> 00:06:51.770
I'm not the one who called you.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.260
Oh, Takahara-san.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:56.990
Could you bring me a muffler?

00:06:56.990 --> 00:06:58.350
Y-Yes.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.370
You moron!

00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:08.830
He's showing promise for sure.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:25.400
But you've sure changed, Komazawa.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.970
How so?

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.200
You wouldn't even talk to Capeta at first.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.440
Our ace hates the FSRS, after all.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:39.150
I still hate that group of slackers.

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:45.310
But Capeta is different.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:46.560
How should I put it...

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:54.630
It's like finding a black rice ball amongst all the pretty, fancy cakes.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:56.350
Huh?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.340
What's with that simile?!

00:07:58.850 --> 00:08:03.530
Because you came from a poor family and your face is ordinary.

00:08:03.530 --> 00:08:06.800
You're also a guy who would mistake a spanner for a frying pan.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.220
In other words, I can't leave you alone!

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:14.390
Thank you very much!

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:16.380
Yo!  Our ace!

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.280
You sure are big-hearted!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:22.510
His driving is something...

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.300
But I wonder why he got dropped for that scholarship.

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:27.450
It's because of his face, of course.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:28.660
Face?

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.620
My face?

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:34.580
Whether you're a sportsman or whatever, nowadays your face decides all.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.300
It makes it easier to get sponsors.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:40.510
Come to think of it, the guy who passed, Shiba...

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:42.470
He's the cool type.

00:08:42.470 --> 00:08:46.200
But surely they wouldn't take looks over driving ability, would they?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.680
It could have been the other way around.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:51.640
But I bet the reason why Shiba passed is because of his appearance.

00:09:00.270 --> 00:09:01.760
Really?!

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:04.410
You really know Monami-chan?!

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:06.700
Yeah.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.850
We live close by and...

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.810
S-So you guys are childhood friends?!

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:11.370
Yeah.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:15.020
That sounds like a bittersweet story.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:16.500
You!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.130
You're doing that too much.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:19.530
It's okay.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:22.960
It annoys me that he's childhood friends with an idol when he only has an ordinary face like this.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:26.280
Our ace's face is turning all red.

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:28.530
Could it be that you're a fan of Monami?

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.260
Listen up, Capeta.  Things like this shouldn't distract us drivers.

00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:34.230
So you are a fan.

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:36.700
Capeta, could you get me her autograph next time?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.440
A-Autograph?!

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:40.260
Well...

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.150
She's kinda busy right now.

00:09:42.950 --> 00:09:44.650
"She," huh?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:47.280
So that means you're more than childhood friends, but not quite a couple, huh?

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:49.790
Knock it off!

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:50.460
All right.

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.120
How long are you guys going to be chatting?

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.140
Lunch break is over.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.700
Yes.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.340
Thank you!

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:07.520
Do your best, Monami!

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:08.440
Thank you!

00:10:08.440 --> 00:10:10.330
I'll do my best!

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.200
Thank you!  Thank you!

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.310
Thank you!  Thank you!

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:18.790
For now, the car is the only place you'll be able to rest.

00:10:20.200 --> 00:10:21.680
So what do you think?

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.780
I feel spaced out!

00:10:25.690 --> 00:10:29.290
<i>I bet you're busy and having a hard time, but let's fight on!</i>

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:30.910
<i>Capeta is also working hard.</i>

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:34.420
<i>Even though we're apart, we're still Team Capeta!!</i>

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:39.050
<i>P.S. There are slick people in the entertainment business, so be careful.</i>

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.970
I'd sure like an autograph.

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:45.110
Oh.  It's from Monami.

00:10:45.110 --> 00:10:46.050
What?!

00:10:46.050 --> 00:10:48.570
Ca-chan, good luck on your debut race!

00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:51.680
Rev your engine to the max and beat that kabuki-face!

00:10:51.680 --> 00:10:52.810
Damn you, Capeta!

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:55.530
F-Forward that message to me!

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:57.730
Huh?  Huh?  Forward it?

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:20.230
This is only a free drive, but he's still giving it everything he's got.

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:22.610
He's had 6 wins in 6 races since his debut.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:24.180
Just as we hoped.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.390
I heard we've had contact from a team in France.

00:11:27.390 --> 00:11:29.100
We've also heard from Italy.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:32.130
They said, "Please send us Naomi Minamoto's profile."

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:35.160
So his road to the wide world is opening.

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:39.140
Well, drivers like him only come around once every 10 years.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.670
Yeah.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:44.310
And if we had one more, things would sure get exciting.

00:11:44.930 --> 00:11:46.090
One more?

00:11:46.090 --> 00:11:48.780
Well, there was one other, wasn't there?

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:50.370
Forwarding.  Forwarding...

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:51.240
Forwarding.  Forwarding...

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:54.400
Oh.  It disappeared.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.450
You can't even use a mobile phone?!

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:01.910
<i>Hurry up and get here!</i>

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:24.920
Good morning!  Good morning!  Good morning!

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.380
Good morning!  Good morning!  Good morning!

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:27.590
Good morning!  Good morning!  Good morning!

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:36.570
At last.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.060
Oh man!  I overslept!

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:49.530
Starting today, Capeta will finally be a legit FSte driver!

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.490
One, two.  One, two.  One, two.

00:12:52.490 --> 00:12:53.610
One, two.  One, two.  One, two.

00:12:53.610 --> 00:12:54.380
One, two.  One, two.  One, two.

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:59.150
Today is the day that kabuki-face is going to say bye to the world!

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:03.520
If they race together, Ca-chan will be the fastest!

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.510
Good morning!

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:13.450
I'm sorry!

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:14.650
I overslept!

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.520
Huh?

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:04.450
Sixty... three.

00:14:04.450 --> 00:14:05.000
Sixty... three.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:07.130
It's my number!

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:11.290
Capeta!

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:13.500
It's my name!

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:19.720
It's my machine!

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:30.470
This is my machine!

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:31.540
That's right.

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.200
From this day on, that's your partner.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:40.330
Happy 16th birthday, Capeta!

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:45.290
So you're now officially a Persec FSte driver.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.080
We have high expectations of you.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:51.040
It's finally the 16th birthday you've been waiting for.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:52.780
Congratulations.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:54.550
This is your license.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:00.680
Thank you very much!

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:03.220
It's my license!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.550
Let's see.

00:15:05.220 --> 00:15:08.280
You look so grown up there.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:10.980
That photo of you looks a bit more upright.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.440
No, it looks like you're the representative of the common people.

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:17.800
All right.

00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:20.360
Let's set up Capeta's seat before his debut race.

00:15:20.930 --> 00:15:21.890
Yes!

00:15:21.890 --> 00:15:23.320
All right!

00:15:25.460 --> 00:15:29.540
Your debut race is going to be at that destined Shizuoka International Circuit.

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:30.690
Yes!

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:34.120
The home straight there is long, and it also slopes downward.

00:15:34.120 --> 00:15:38.010
Plus, the R in the first corner is tough and deep.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:38.710
Ow!

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.940
In other words, it's difficult, right?

00:15:40.940 --> 00:15:42.750
Yes.  It's difficult.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:48.430
Just don't chicken out on that corner.  Dive in, slowly speed down, and turn.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:50.540
In other words, attack it with your fighting spirit.

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:51.740
That's the only way.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.840
But I'll say one thing, Capeta.

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:58.190
There's a big difference between the kart you've been driving and the Formula.

00:15:58.700 --> 00:16:00.580
It's war in the Formula.

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.340
Don't you forget that.

00:16:02.340 --> 00:16:03.160
Yes!

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.990
<i>I can finally fight him.</i>

00:16:06.780 --> 00:16:08.870
<i>I've chased him for a long time.</i>

00:16:12.030 --> 00:16:14.500
<i>For the first time, on the same stage...</i>

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:18.580
<i>I can finally fight him!</i>

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:35.980
All right!

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:37.300
Finally!

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:39.400
It's your debut race!

00:16:39.400 --> 00:16:41.870
Don't get all nervous, okay?

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.780
I'm here to support you!

00:16:45.170 --> 00:16:47.110
What's the point of you getting all nervous?

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:49.470
We're counting on you, ace.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:53.510
<i>Taira Capeta.</i>

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.250
<i>I won't lose to you here.</i>

00:16:59.780 --> 00:17:01.040
Mom...

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.850
Our Capeta has finally... finally...!

00:17:04.350 --> 00:17:07.100
He's lucky his debut race is here.

00:17:07.100 --> 00:17:10.100
He knows this course already, so there's a chance for him.

00:17:10.830 --> 00:17:13.100
Don't forget the three rules, Capeta.

00:17:13.940 --> 00:17:16.560
We have to produce results in this debut race!

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.910
<i>It's finally time, Capeta-kun.</i>

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:26.360
<i>I'm looking forward to seeing how you drive today.</i>

00:17:30.430 --> 00:17:31.240
<i>All right!</i>

00:17:31.240 --> 00:17:32.430
<i>I'll do it!</i>

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:33.370
Hey.

00:17:33.730 --> 00:17:35.140
Shiba.

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:46.520
To be honest...

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:48.840
I thought I could be more of a match.

00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:53.140
You'll know when you drive against him.

00:17:54.360 --> 00:17:55.060
He's...

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:56.920
a monster.

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:00.480
It hit me when I drove with Sam's on the first day.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:03.240
It's best if you forget about all your naive dreams.

00:18:06.970 --> 00:18:08.350
I'm no match for him right now.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.780
But...

00:18:10.550 --> 00:18:12.490
I'll be the one who beats him!

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:20.130
<i>I'll also beat him.</i>

00:18:21.050 --> 00:18:22.710
<i>In this race!</i>

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:26.170
<b>We will start the free practice momentarily.</b>

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:30.140
<i>Taira, who I've chased since his karting days, is finally...</i>

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:32.100
<i>finally making a debut in the Formula!</i>

00:18:32.100 --> 00:18:34.140
<i>This is exciting.</i>

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:37.210
For the time being, keep yourself within the 45-second range.

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:39.100
That's how it is, so give it all you got!

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:40.180
Yes!

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:47.780
Keeping within the 45-second range is going to be a severe hurdle.

00:18:47.780 --> 00:18:50.780
Well, nothing's going to happen unless he tries.

00:18:53.890 --> 00:18:54.900
He's out!

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.250
Capeta!

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:05.220
<i>All right.</i>

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:05.880
<i>I'm counting on you!</i>

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:18.930
He's looking good!

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.020
Capeta!

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:28.100
<i>Good.</i>

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:29.390
<i>Just as I imagined.</i>

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:30.860
<i>You're very responsive.</i>

00:19:35.830 --> 00:19:37.790
<i>You're coming in at full speed already, huh?</i>

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:41.250
<i>I can do it... with you!</i>

00:19:45.710 --> 00:19:48.460
<i>This world isn't that easy!</i>

00:19:55.030 --> 00:19:58.570
Do you think Capeta's driving as if he's in the race already?

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:00.700
Yeah.  The beginning is always important.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.040
He has to go at that rate.

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:05.690
Start with a bang and leave a strong impression!

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:08.000
That's good!  That's good, Ryou!

